# Cliffhangers. A `hook` is the last line of its flight day; its resolver (`due`,
# `when fired <hook>`) opens the next day. The engine spaces hooks >= 4 days apart.
# Resolutions: mostly satisfying, sometimes ominous, never "it was nothing".
# All hooks share hook_who to carry the astronaut over; they never overlap.
# House style: content/STYLE.md.

# --- 1. Emergency band ---------------------------------------------------------
card h_band
type event
cat mystery
hook
once
days 30 33
weight 10
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text At 23:40 {A}'s dish logs a burst on the old common channel. The bearing is Mars, near enough; at this range the dish can't say more.

card r_band
type event
cat mystery
clue
due
once
days 31 34
roles A
when fired h_band
when is A hook_who
text {A} decodes it: a safe-mode beacon asking for instructions no one sent. It cuts off at the same byte every time, before the spacecraft ID; a sweeping beam would clip it somewhere new each turn. {A} notes it, and still bets on the relay.
do trait A curious 3
do morale A 4

# --- 2. Cabin pressure -------------------------------------------------------
card h_pressure
type event
cat repair
hook
once
days 4 35
weight 10
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text 01:50. The cabin pressure on {A}'s ship has started to fall. Slowly. {A} is the only one awake.

card r_pressure
type event
cat repair
due
once
days 5 36
roles A
when fired h_pressure
when is A hook_who
text {A} spent four hours with an ultrasonic leak detector and a roll of tape. The culprit was a cable feedthrough whose seal shrank in the cold of the shaded side. It's resealed, the pressure holds, and the trend line is taped above the console like a fish someone caught.
do res spares -1
do morale A 5

# --- 3. Solar flare ----------------------------------------------------------
card h_flare
type event
cat grim
hook
once
days 7 33
weight 9
roles A
when cond A ok
when !fired storm_shelter
do who hook_who A
text 23:52. The space weather feed flags a major flare on the Sun. Its protons will reach the fleet in about forty minutes. {A} starts calling the other ships.

card r_flare
type event
cat grim
due
once
days 8 34
roles A
when fired h_flare
when is A hook_who
text Every crew spent the night in their storm shelter between the water tanks, seven faces in a video grid, listening to the dosimeters tick. By morning the fleet had taken a month's dose in six hours. {A} logged the peak and slept until noon.
do var storms 1
do morale A 3

# --- 4. Uncommanded thruster --------------------------------------------------
card h_thruster
type event
cat repair skill
hook
once
days 4 35
weight 10
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text 02:14. A thruster on {A}'s ship fires without a command. Then another. {A} is already at the console.

card r_thruster
type event
cat repair skill
due
once
days 5 36
roles A
when fired h_thruster
when is A hook_who
lean brave manual watch
text By 02:30 the ship was steady again.
option manual | Hand control | {A} took attitude into manual, just for a minute, and held it by hand while the valve telemetry scrolled past. One valve reported "closed" while it leaked. It's isolated now, and the log of the night is a single calm page.
  trait A brave 2
  morale A 4
  set valve_out
  who valve_who A
  mark t_valve
  res fuel -1
option watch | Isolate and watch | {A} let the control loop fight it and watched the pulses, counting. Every one traced to a single valve that reported "closed" while it leaked. It's isolated now, and the plot of the night is pinned up with the leak circled in red.
  trait A curious 2
  morale A 4
  set valve_out
  who valve_who A
  mark t_valve
  res fuel -1

card valve_later
type event
cat repair
due
once
days 24 33
roles A
when flag valve_out
when is A valve_who
when since t_valve >= 6
text Every attitude move on {A}'s ship now takes a beat longer, routed around the valve that was isolated that night. The flight software has a new line in it with {A}'s initials. {A} has stopped noticing, mostly, except at 02:00.
do morale A -1

# --- 5. Alarm flood -----------------------------------------------------------
card h_flood
type event
cat repair skill
hook
once
days 4 35
weight 10
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text Just before midnight, 214 alarms hit {A}'s console at once. One of them is real.

card r_flood
type event
cat repair skill
due
once
days 5 36
roles A
when fired h_flood
when is A hook_who
text {A} found it at 01:30, buried on page nine: a coolant pump drawing too much current, minutes from tripping. {A} swapped to the backup before the primary died. By morning the alarm list had been cut from 214 to a page, and nobody is sure when {A} slept.
do morale A 5
do res spares -1

# --- 6. Ground silence --------------------------------------------------------
card h_silence
type event
cat grim
hook
once
days 10 35
weight 8
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text Mission Control misses a scheduled check-in. Then the next one. {A} sends a third hail and starts the clock: twice the light time, plus a minute for someone to put a coffee down.

card r_silence
type event
cat grim
due
once
days 11 36
roles A
when fired h_silence
when is A hook_who
text The reply arrived at 06:12. A ground station had gone down in a storm at home, and the backup had to wait for Earth to turn. The message ends: "All good here. How are you?" {A} reads it slowly before answering.
do morale A 6
do trait A warm 2

# --- 7. Hull strike -----------------------------------------------------------
card h_strike
type event
cat grim
hook
once
days 4 35
weight 9
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text Something hits {A}'s ship hard enough to ring the hull like a bell. Every pressure reading is green. {A} doesn't trust green.

card r_strike
type event
cat grim
due
once
days 5 36
roles A
when fired h_strike
when is A hook_who
text The morning EVA found a crater the size of a fingernail in a shield panel, and behind it, nothing. The shielding did its job. {A} photographed it next to a ruler, and the anomaly report finally has a good picture.
do trait A brave 2
do morale A 3

# --- 8. Star tracker ghost (ominous) ---------------------------------------------
card h_ghost
type event
cat mystery
hook
once
days 25 33
weight 8
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text {A}'s star tracker flags a catalog mismatch: one star too many in the field. On the next frame, it has moved.

card r_ghost
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 26 34
roles A
when fired h_ghost
when is A hook_who
text {A} pinned it down by morning: a launch cover plate shed by one of the fleet's own ships at departure, turning end over end along almost the same path. It will pass forty kilometres off the bow. It has drifted alongside them the whole way, and no one is coming for it.
do trait A curious 3
do morale A -2


# --- 9. A voice on the loop ----------------------------------------------------------
card h_voice
type event
cat mystery
hook
once
days 25 33
weight 10
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text 02:40. The intercom on {A}'s ship opens by itself and plays four seconds of a kitchen somewhere: a kettle, a radio, someone laughing. {A} is the only one aboard.

card r_voice
type event
cat human
due
once
days 26 34
roles A
when fired h_voice
when is A hook_who
text {A} traced it by dawn: a message from home, recorded the night before launch and set to play on this flight day, then mangled by the galley-screen update. The rest of it plays at breakfast, kettle and all. {A} listens with the volume very low.
do morale A 6
do trait A warm 3

# --- 10. A ship drops off the net -------------------------------------------------
card h_dark
type event
cat mystery
hook
once
days 25 33
weight 8
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text 23:58. {A}'s ship stops answering on the fleet net in the middle of a sentence. No telemetry, just an empty slot on six displays, and out of the windows its cabin lights burning as usual.

card r_dark
type event
cat mystery
clue core key
due
once
days 26 34
roles A
when fired h_dark
when is A hook_who
text {A} came back at 05:58. The comms computer had hung on a link request from Mars, signed with an old program key the fleet trusts, until the six-hour lost-link timer rebooted it. Sequence number 1, as if the sender were new; the challenge, new too. "Not ours," says the ground. A key ticket opens.
do trait A brave 3
do morale A -2
